check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5707078Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5720344Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5824820Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5835714Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5836474Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5837359Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5837801Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5838454Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5839415Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5839984Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5840421Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5841615Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5841990Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5843551Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5851117Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5852099Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5853120Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5853681Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5854018Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5854389Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5854634Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5855042Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5855193Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5855308Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5855479Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5855868Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5856364Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5856581Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5856689Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5856908Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5857127Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5857595Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5858030Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5858835Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5859161Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5859484Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5859920Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5860330Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5864340Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5865040Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5877222Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5877797Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5878539Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5879784Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5880477Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5899584Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5900201Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5911128Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5911726Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5912462Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5912846Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5913143Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5913604Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5913971Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5914736Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5915153Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-05T02:30:07.5915375Z If you would like to
